  "A missing word caused a deadly train crash.",
  "On November 21, 1950, two trains collided near Valemount, Canada.",
  "The head-on crash killed 17 soldiers and 4 crew members.",
  "Investigators found a telegraph operator sent an incomplete order.",
  "He faced manslaughter charges but was acquitted by his lawyer, John Diefenbaker.",
  "Afterward, the railway finally installed better safety signals."
